Prompts the user to either start the game or quit
  - Close the program on quit
When the game is started, short cutscene plays with the initial story

Then for the next 4 floors:
User chooses 1 of three doors in the dungeon

  If user chooses a item door:
    Add item to Inventory Class’ abilities, weapons or consumables ArrayLists<Enum> and continue to next floor
  
  If user selects a combat door:
    Prompt user to select a weapon and 3 abilities to use in the fight
    Add the selected abilities to the curr_abilites ArrayList<Abilities> in the Inventory and set the curr_weapon to the selected Weapon object
    Enter combat system

  Combat System:
    Start with the user’s turn, where they can either block, use their weapon, use an ability, use an item or retreat.
      - Block will completely negate damage if player defense level is greater than enemy offense level and does half damage if enemy offense level is greater than player defense level
      - Weapon skills will deal damage on hit with various damage types
          If the enemy’s type weakness corresponds to the weapons damage type, the weapon will deal more damage
          If the enemy’s strength corresponds to the weapon damage, the weapon deals less damage
      - Using an ability will apply a status effect associated with said ability onto the enemy
      - Using an item will heal the player for the the amount associated with the Consumable object
      - A retreat will cause the player to lose the encounter, while still progressing to the next door
    After user turn, enemy will perform a random skill on the player
      - Enemy can also block with the same rules as player
    During each turn, any status effects on the enemies will activate
      - Bleed deals flat damage on the use of a skill
      - Rupture deals flat damage when hit
      - Freeze will cause the player to be unable to move next turn
      - Paralyze will hinder the player from using combat or block skills and take bonus dmg
      - Burn deals fixed damage at turn end
    Exit combat if either the enemy or the player loses, although exit the game on player death
      - If player wins, gain currency Items and defense + offense level
      - If player loses, gain nothing

  After combat, a short cutscene plays furthering the story

When the player reaches the final floor:
  User selects their items
  A short cutscene plays introducing, the boss enemy
  User can choose to either fight the boss, or bribe the boss with money if they have enough
    If the user bribes the boss, the game will output another short cutscene, then end the game
    If user chooses to fight the boss, enter combat with the enemy
      - If player wins, play a short cutscene and end the game
